  "body": " Projection onto the -plane  Projection Orthogonal projection  Orthogonal projection onto the -plane   Let . Describe the function geometrically.    In the equation , the input vector and the output vector are both in . First we multiply by a vector to see what it does: . Multiplication by simply sets the -coordinate equal to zero: it projects vertically onto the -plane .              Multiplication by the matrix projects a vector onto the -plane. Move the input vector to see how the output vector changes.     "
