  "body": " Verifying linearity: rotation   Define by . Verify that is linear.    Since is defined geometrically, we give a geometric argument. For the first property, is the sum of the vectors obtained by rotating and by . On the other side of the equation, is the vector obtained by rotating the sum of the vectors and . But it does not matter whether we sum or rotate first, as the following picture shows. \\usetikzlibrary{angles}              For the second property, is the vector obtained by rotating by the angle , then changing its length by a factor of (reversing direction of . On the other hand, first changes the length of , then rotates. But it does not matter in which order we do these two operations. \\usetikzlibrary{angles}              This verifies that is a linear transformation. We will find its matrix in the next . Note however that it is not at all obvious that can be expressed as multiplication by a matrix.   "
