  "body": " Order of Operations  Matrix multiplication order of operations  Transformation composition of order of operations  Let and be linear transformations, and let and be their standard matrices, respectively. Recall that is the vector obtained by first applying to , and then .  On the matrix side, the standard matrix of is the product , so . By associativity of matrix multiplication, we have , so the product can be computed by first multiplying by , then multipyling the product by .  Therefore, matrix multiplication happens in the same order as composition of transformations. In other words, both matrices and transformations are written in the order opposite from the order in which they act. But matrix multiplication and composition of transformations are written in the same order as each other: the matrix for is .  "
